course: dictionary
lesson: 13996
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning the writer wants. «The news report said heavy losses were felt after the battle.» Here losses means soldiers or people who were killed or hurt in war.
explain: «The shop made losses of two thousand pounds last year.» The words shop and pounds are clues: losses means money a business has lost. «Our team had only two losses all season.» Now losses means games that were lost.
explain: Officials and newspapers often use losses to talk about deaths in war without saying «killed». Read the clues around the word, then swap in your meaning to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Losses is a plural noun. The singular is a loss.
fact: «Losses» can mean soldiers or people killed or wounded in a war or a disaster.
fact: «Losses» can mean money a business loses. It is the opposite of profits.
fact: «Losses» can mean games that were lost, or things that were lost.
fact: In news about war, losses is a gentle, official way of talking about people who have died.
exercise: «The army reported heavy losses after the battle.» What does losses mean here? | *Soldiers or people killed or wounded | Things found on the field | Games the army won | Money the army spent on boots
exercise: «The shop made losses of two thousand pounds last year.» What does losses mean here? | *Money a business has lost | Football matches that were lost | Soldiers killed in war | Happy customers
exercise: «Our team had only two losses all season.» What does losses mean here? | *Games that were lost | Bags that were stolen | Soldiers in a battle | Money the team earned
test: «The company's losses rose sharply this year.» What does losses mean here? | People killed in an accident | Matches the company won | *Money the company lost | Lost keys and phones
test: «The news said losses were heavy after the flood.» What does losses mean here? | Money the town saved | *People killed or hurt in the disaster | Games cancelled because of rain | Gifts given to the families
exam: «Our losses this season taught us a lot.» What does losses mean here? | Toys we found in the park | Money we earned from the shop | *Games we lost | Soldiers who fought in a battle
